# Temporary/local-only files excluded from distribution
.work/
*.tmp
*.cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.log
.DS_Store

# Large intermediate files
*.parquet
*.sqlite
*.db

# Deliverables that the root Sphinx rule would otherwise exclude
#
# The root .gitignore carries `*.html` at line 36 for the Sphinx build tree, and
# it is a pre-existing rule of the project, so it is left exactly as it is. It
# does, however, also exclude reports/e2e-engineering-document.html, which is the
# deliverable of the html-e2e-engineering-document sprint, and that file would
# therefore never be committed.
#
# This is a path-specific negation rather than `!*.html`. A blanket negation would
# re-include every generated HTML page under docs/artifacts/, which is the class
# of file the root rule exists to keep out: the visual-check scratch output next
# door (docs/artifacts/diagrams/*.visual-check.html) is produced by tooling and
# must stay ignored. Only the one deliverable is named.
#
# No `!reports/` or `!*/` line is needed and none is added: git cannot re-include
# a path whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, but reports/ is not excluded by any
# rule, so the single path negation is sufficient. Verified with
# `git check-ignore -v` on this file and on two controls.
!reports/e2e-engineering-document.html
